/* Shared RmlUi theme for player-facing menus (RmlUi migration, Phase 1).
   Base look + font, imported by each menu's own .rcss.

   ── AESTHETIC ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Gruvbox-dark palette (warm cream text on dark brown-grey, yellow accent),
   squared corners, weathered-brown frame, plus subtle CRT post-effects (text
   glow + scanlines + vignette). The ornate riveted frame is a Phase-4 ninepatch
   drop-in (see .panel); the CSS here approximates it with a squared border + a
   recessed vignette. Scanlines/vignette are driven from C++ (see .crt).

   ── PALETTE (single source of truth, gruvbox) ─────────────────────────────
   RCSS in RmlUi 6.2 has NO var()/custom properties (only @keyframes, @decorator,
   @spritesheet, @media), so these values cannot be deduplicated into tokens —
   they must be repeated literally wherever used. This block is the canonical
   reference: when a menu's .rcss needs one of these roles, copy the hex from
   here, and when a colour changes, change every copy to match this table.

     role               hex          gruvbox      used for
     ----------------   ----------   ----------   --------------------------------
     panel-bg           {{bg}}    bg0_h        .panel background
     frame / border     {{bg4}}    bg4          panel border, separators
     frame-inner        {{bg2}}    bg2          inner double-border line (Phase-4)
     scrollbar          {{bg3}}    bg3          scrollbar sliderbar
     scrollbar-hover    {{gray}}    gray         scrollbar sliderbar :hover
     text-primary       {{fg}}    fg1          body text (cascades — don't re-declare)
     text-muted         {{fg4}}    fg4          secondary columns, filter line
     text-disabled      {{bg3}}    bg3          disabled rows
     text-bright        {{fg0}}    fg0          hovered item text
     accent             {{yellow}}    yellow       titles, hotkeys, selected-item background
     on-accent          {{bg-hard}}    bg0_h        text on an accent background
     item-bg            {{bg1}}    bg1          selectable row / button background
     item-hover-bg      {{bg2}}    bg2          selectable row / button :hover background
     danger / hp-red    {{red}}    red          HP bar fill, failures (domain colour, per-screen)

   The item-bg/hover/accent "selectable item" triad is shared by uilist rows
   and query_popup buttons via the .item class below — change those states
   there, not per-component. */

/* Lengths are in `dp` (density-independent px), not `px`: the RmlUi context is
   sized in physical pixels, so dp + the context density ratio (set in
   rmlui_layer::new_frame) keeps fonts/spacing the intended size on HiDPI. */
body {
    font-family: "Terminus (TTF)";
    font-size: 18dp;
    color: {{fg}};
}

/* Title / header role — yellow accent with a CRT glow. Opt-in (screens that want
   it add class="title"); not forced, so eyeballed screens don't regress. Glow is
   kept off body text on purpose: a glow under dense lists muddies them (see
   advinv/inventory). Tune the glow radius/alpha here. */
.title {
    color: {{yellow}};
    font-effect: glow( 2dp {{yellow-glow}} );
}

/* Dark squared panel shared by all menus. Gruvbox bg + squared brown border + a
   recessed vignette. The vignette (and scanlines) are radial/linear GRADIENT
   decorators, driven live from C++ (rmlui_layer::apply_crt) on every .panel and
   the .crt overlay — gradients render via the interface's CompileShader pipeline.
   The static decorator below is the fallback when C++ isn't driving it.

   Scanlines are NOT here: a decorator paints behind the element's own content, so
   they'd never cross the text. They go on the `.crt` overlay (drawn on top).

   Phase-4 drop-in (ornate riveted frame): slice assets/frame.png as a 9-patch
   and replace `border` with, e.g.:
       decorator: ninepatch( "assets/frame.png", 16px 16px / 16px 16px ); */
.panel {
    background-color: {{bg}};
    border: 2dp {{bg4}};
    border-radius: 0;
    padding: 12dp;
    decorator: radial-gradient( farthest-corner, #00000000, #00000077 );
}

/* CRT overlay — a click-through layer drawn ON TOP, masked to the active panel so
   its scanlines cross the bright text. Opt-in: add a bare
   <div id="crt-overlay" class="crt"/> as the last child of a screen's <body>.

   Geometry (sized to the panel rect), the scanline gradient, the scroll and the
   flicker are driven LIVE from C++ each frame (rmlui_layer::apply_crt, fed by the
   F4 "CRT" sliders), set as inline RCSS — so they tune in-game without a reload.
   This rule only owns click-through + stacking. Once dialled in, bake the chosen
   gradient strings back here as a static decorator. */
.crt {
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 10;
}

/* GOTCHA (bit diary + mutations): RmlUi elements default to `display: inline`.
   The familiar `div { display: block }` lives in RmlUi's SAMPLE rml.rcss, which
   we do NOT link — so a bare `<div>` row flows inline and a list renders as one
   wrapped paragraph. A list row must EITHER set `display: block`/`flex` itself,
   OR be a child of a `display: flex; flex-direction: column` container (flex
   items get blockified). The `.item` class below does NOT set display — set it
   on your row class (see .diary-line / .mut-line, or uilist .item). */

/* Selectable item — shared by uilist rows and query_popup buttons. The
   component keeps its own layout (padding/flex/margin); this owns the palette
   and the interactive states. :hover is declared before .selected so keyboard
   selection wins when a selected item is also hovered (equal specificity →
   source order). Base text colour inherits text-primary from body. */
.item {
    background-color: {{bg1}};
    border-radius: 0;
}
.item:hover {
    background-color: {{bg2}};
    color: {{fg0}};
}
.item.selected {
    background-color: {{yellow}};
    color: {{bg-hard}};
}

/* F.2 tab bar (lifted at the 3rd tab use = bionics, after missions + scores both
   shipped a content-switching tab row). A horizontal row of `.tab` items, each a
   `.item` (so it inherits the bg/:hover/.selected triad); `.tab.selected` adds
   bold. Bind tabs as a Vector of {name, selected} and switch the active one from
   C++ on click (keyboard owns LEFT/RIGHT). missions/scores keep their own copies
   (.missions-tab / .scores-tab) — adopt this on their next touch, don't retrofit
   eyeballed screens. The 1dp brown border gives each tab a squared bracket box. */
.tabs {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    margin-bottom: 8dp;
}
.tab {
    flex: 1;
    padding: 4dp 10dp;
    margin-right: 6dp;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1dp {{bg4}};
}
.tab.selected {
    font-weight: bold;
}

/* F.2 scrolling-text-view seed (extracted at Tier-1 screen #3 = help, where the
   overflow text-pane recurs a 3rd time after missions' .missions-detail and
   scores' .scores-body). A flex child that scrolls its own overflow. The
   explicit `vh` max-height is the ACTUAL scroll bound — RmlUi 6.2 won't constrain
   a flex child's height by its parent alone, so without it the overflow region
   collapses to height 0 and the text is clipped invisible (missions gotcha #1).
   Already-committed screens keep their own copies; adopt this on their next touch
   rather than retrofitting (avoids regressing eyeballed screens for no gain). */
.scroll-pane {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    max-height: 84vh;
    overflow-y: auto;
    padding: 4dp 8dp;
}

/* Scrollbars for any overflowing list. */
scrollbarvertical {
    width: 10dp;
    margin-left: 4dp;
}
scrollbarvertical sliderbar {
    background-color: {{bg3}};
    border-radius: 0;
    min-height: 24dp;
}
scrollbarvertical sliderbar:hover {
    background-color: {{gray}};
}
